From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:01:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: conntrack: take 64-bit counts in nf_ct_acct_add

The flowtable adds the hardware counts of one stats poll to conntrack
in one call, and that call took 32-bit packet and byte counts. A poll
interval that carries 4 GiB or more lost a multiple of 4 GiB.

Conntrack now gets the whole delta of a poll, whatever its size. A
fast flow reaches that size in one interval, and a longer flow
timeout makes the interval longer.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 include/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_acct.h |    3 +--
 net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_core.c         |    3 +--
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/include/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_acct.h
+++ b/include/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_acct.h
@@ -65,8 +65,7 @@ static inline void nf_ct_set_acct(struct
 #endif
 }
 
-void nf_ct_acct_add(struct nf_conn *ct, u32 dir, unsigned int packets,
-		    unsigned int bytes);
+void nf_ct_acct_add(struct nf_conn *ct, u32 dir, u64 packets, u64 bytes);
 
 static inline void nf_ct_acct_update(struct nf_conn *ct, u32 dir,
 				     unsigned int bytes)
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_core.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_core.c
@@ -917,8 +917,7 @@ out:
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(nf_conntrack_hash_check_insert);
 
-void nf_ct_acct_add(struct nf_conn *ct, u32 dir, unsigned int packets,
-		    unsigned int bytes)
+void nf_ct_acct_add(struct nf_conn *ct, u32 dir, u64 packets, u64 bytes)
 {
 	struct nf_conn_acct *acct;
 
